    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #318\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-82-implementation-audit-fixes-03-23-enforc-thr_pq3qj62wc8`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis closes the final part of the relation-integrity work (#211 → #212 → #82) by enforcing cardinality under concurrency and repairing canonical relation-property config.\n\n- **Cardinality enforcement** (`0013_relation_cardinality.sql`): a `BEFORE INSERT` trigger on `item_relations` takes a transaction-scoped `pg_advisory_xact_lock` keyed on `relation_definition_id`, then rejects a conflicting edge per the declared cardinality — `one_to_one` forbids reusing either `item_a` or `item_b`, `one_to_many` forbids `item_a` from getting a second edge, `many_to_many` is unconstrained. The advisory lock serializes concurrent inserts for the same definition so two racing transactions can't both pass the check under read-committed isolation. A new `CardinalityViolationError` (409, `cardinality_violation`) surfaces this.\n- **Config repair migration** (`0014_relation_config_repair.sql`): scans every `relation_definitions` row, backfills/repairs paired properties' `targetDatabaseId` from the opposite side's `database_id`, and validates one-way properties' existing target — aborting with the offending property id on any missing/invalid/inconsistent data.\n- **Real bug fixed along the way**: `Emails.attachments` was declared `one_to_many`, but that direction is structurally incompatible with \"one email, many attachment files\" and has no inverse to swap onto (Files' schema is locked). Corrected to `many_to_many` in `seedEmailModule.ts` — it never had a real constraint to lose, since each attachment always gets a fresh Files item.\n- Added 12 new integration tests covering every cardinality, concurrency races, invalid target databases, locked-creation config completeness, and migration repair/abort behavior.\n\nVerified: full monorepo build, migration-numbering check, dependency-boundaries check, and the complete test suite (83 unit + 415 integration + 5 e2e tests) all green, with no regressions.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
