    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #318\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to the same branch: `bb/relay-82-implementation-audit-fixes-03-23-enforc-thr_pq3qj62wc8` (existing PR #318).\n\n## Summary\n\nAddressed the code review finding on PR #318: the `one_to_many` concurrency test relied on a 100ms `setTimeout` to sequence the two racing clients, which could invert under CI load. Replaced it with an explicit `pg_advisory_xact_lock` acquired by the winning client up front (the same lock key the trigger itself uses) — Postgres advisory locks are reentrant within one session/transaction, so the winning client's own insert still proceeds immediately, while the losing client is now guaranteed to block until the winner commits, regardless of timing. Also added a matching `one_to_one` race case (same `item_b`, different `item_a`), per the review's low-priority coverage note.\n\nVerified: full monorepo build, migration-numbering check, dependency-boundaries check, and the complete test suite (83 unit + 416 integration + 5 e2e) all green, no regressions.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
