    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #318\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to the same branch: `bb/relay-82-implementation-audit-fixes-03-23-enforc-thr_pq3qj62wc8` (existing PR #318).\n\n## Summary\n\nAddressed the review's blocking finding and low-priority suggestion on PR #318:\n\n- **Semantic inversion fixed (blocking)**: the trigger had `one_to_many` backwards — it capped `item_a` to one edge, but the issue's contract puts `property_id_a`/`item_a` on the \"one\" side (allowed many `item_b` edges), with the uniqueness constraint landing on `item_b`. Flipped the trigger logic and its tests to match.\n- **Seed data corrected accordingly**: this direction requires `property_id_a` to be the side whose own field is genuinely single-valued. Swapped source/inverse for the five paired relations where it mattered (`Tasks.project`/`Projects.tasks`, `Projects.area`/`Areas.projects` \"Hub\", `Projects.company`/`Companies.projects`, `Events.project`/`Projects.events`, `Folders.mailbox`/`Mailboxes.folders`). For one-directional relations that can't be swapped (`Emails.attachments`, `Files.area`, `Journal.area`, `Inbox.type`, `Inbox.journalDay`, Processing proposals' `sourceInbox`/`sourceTranscript`), corrected the declared cardinality to `many_to_many`, since none of them ever had a real single-edge invariant to enforce.\n- **Trigger idempotency (low priority)**: added `DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS` before `CREATE TRIGGER` so the migration is safely re-runnable.\n\nVerified: full monorepo build, migration-numbering check, dependency-boundaries check, and the complete test suite (83 unit + 416 integration + 5 e2e) all green.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
